WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.350
If you want to hear the three, by far, scariest
things to have ever existed in the Wizarding

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.780
World then stick around to the end of this
video.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:17.010
Welcome to Creepy Things, a series where I
take a look at some of the scariest moments

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.210
in non-horror franchises and analyse what
makes them so frightening.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:25.029
The Harry Potter franchise has always been
known for having some of the most disturbing

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:28.750
creatures, so let’s start by exploring a
few of those.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.110
This will contain spoilers for the Harry Potter
series.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:36.021
Not everything I discuss is inherently harmful,
but that doesn’t mean fans won’t find

00:00:36.021 --> 00:00:37.160
it creepy.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.200
When it comes to thestrals, I find it perfectly
understandable that people would be put off

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.200
by them.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.100
Thestrals are bony, skeletal, horses with
huge bat-wings and reptile like faces with

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.940
expressionless eyes.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.460
In addition to their sinister appearance,
they only appear to those that have witnessed

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.220
and comprehended death.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.710
In this sense, they exist as a metaphor for
grievance.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.440
Someone who has witnessed death may try to
explain their appearance to another, but it

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.620
would be impossible to appreciate how creepy
they are without witnessing death and seeing

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.480
them for yourself.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.260
This is also the reason that Harry Potter
and Luna Lovegood are able to bond over the

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.500
fact that both can see the thestrals, because
both have suffered and they can understand

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.760
each other’s pain.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.650
The thestrals at Hogwarts are well trained
and are responsible for transporting the thestral

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.560
drawn carriages around campus.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.922
However, thestrals in the wild can be much
more dangerous -- they are described to have

00:01:26.922 --> 00:01:31.890
sharp fangs to seize and slash their pray,
they are extremely intelligent, and, as we

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:36.270
see when Luna goes out to feed the thestrals,
they are carnivorous, and attracted to the

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.870
smell of blood.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.000
Trolls.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.880
One of the first creatures encountered in
the series.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:50.420
They can be about 12 feet tall, weigh over
1 ton, and have immense strength.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.200
The characters encounter a troll set loose
into Hogwarts their first year.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.420
The troll was set loose by Professor Quirrell
in an attempt to create a distraction so that

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.479
he could steal the Sorcerer's Stone.

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:04.000
Or Philosopher’s Stone, depending on where
you’re from.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.040
The creepiest part about the troll is the
sound it makes.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.050
*roar*

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:14.530
Trolls aren’t capable of intelligent language,
so their cries are really just expressions

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.680
of their hunger for human flesh.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.811
That’s right, these things may not be the
smartest, but they actually eat people, so

00:02:21.811 --> 00:02:26.620
you can only imagine how scary it is for a
child as young as 11 years old to have to

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.450
take one of these on alone.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:33.209
This incident also took place on Halloween,
so also not knowing if this was some kind

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:38.040
of cruel first-year prank or an actual attack
is also bound to cause anxiety.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.360
One good thing to come out of it was that
the scary incident may have been what brought

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:48.260
Harry, Ron and Hermione together as friends,
but there would be many more far scarier opponents

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.310
in the future.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.900
“Not many first year students could take
on a fully grown mountain troll and live to

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:54.900
tell the tale.”

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.790
Cerberus.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:02.599
A cerberus only ever appears during Harry’s
first year.

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:07.040
The one encountered is a giant three-headed
dog with sharp teeth; very aggressive and

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.800
very territorial.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.900
The whole point of having this dog is to scare
students away, as the dog was the guard of

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.790
the door leading to the Philosopher’s Stone.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:20.070
The only thing that’s not scary about this
creature is it’s name: Fluffy.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.840
There are two main factors that make Fluffy
creepy, the first is that the students are

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.660
not told that he is there to guard a door
-- only that they are forbidden from entering

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:28.870
the room.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:33.319
Fluffy falls asleep in the presence of music,
so trying to sneak past him is extremely nerve-wracking,

00:03:33.319 --> 00:03:37.000
because it’s hard to say when he might wake
up and attack.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.510
“Does it seem a bit quiet to you?”

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:47.460
“The harp, it’s stopped playing!”

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.650
*GROWL*

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.099
The Tale of the Three Brothers.

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:54.569
The book is a fairy tale that witches and
wizards apparently tell to their young as

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:59.900
a supposed backstory of the Deathly Hallows,
the most powerful tools in the wizard world.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:04.660
Why any parent would tell this horrifying
tale to their young children who can’t even

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:10.650
read yet, is completely beyond me, but nonetheless,
Ron claims that learning this tale from a

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.400
very young age is commonplace.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:18.299
The story is about three brothers who cheat
death… yes, the grim reaper, and are each

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:20.810
allowed one wish as prize.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.020
The first gets The Elder Wand, the most powerful
wand in existence.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:29.139
The second gets a resurrection stone to bring
someone back to life.

00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:34.449
And the third brother, the wisest of the three
gets the cloak of invisibility to evade death

00:04:34.449 --> 00:04:36.380
in the future.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.199
But that’s not the scary part.

00:04:38.199 --> 00:04:42.319
The first brother uses the Elder wand to kill
a wizard he didn’t like, but because he

00:04:42.319 --> 00:04:47.270
boasted about the power of the wand, someone
came and slit his throat in the night to steal

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:48.270
it.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:51.930
The second brother is the most disturbing
though, he uses the resurrection stone to

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.249
bring back his dead girlfriend.

00:04:54.249 --> 00:04:59.389
She, not belonging in the world and living
appears in a cold sad state, which eventually

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:02.240
drives the brother to kill himself.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.180
Think about the implications of this.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:09.139
Harry uses the resurrection stone to bring
back himself after he allows Voldemort to

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:10.939
kill him in the forest.

00:05:10.939 --> 00:05:15.400
That means it’s possible that if the effects
of taking someone back from death are true,

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:19.939
then Harry will be miserable for his remaining
days, possibly driving his wife and three

00:05:19.939 --> 00:05:22.319
kids mad with his condition.

00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:27.569
Now that doesn’t look to be the case, based
on his behaviour in the epilogue, but it’s

00:05:27.569 --> 00:05:32.039
entirely possible that this will kick in when
his natural lifespan is up, and Ginny’s

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:38.460
final days with Harry will be filled with
misery until Harry seeks his own tragic death.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:47.180
While we’re on the topic of death, it seems
that death is not always the end in the world

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.180
of wizards.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:52.229
There are many ghosts present in the series,
and most of them are completely friendly and

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:54.550
not really creepy in the slightest.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.909
There are, however, a few exceptions.

00:05:58.909 --> 00:06:01.249
*scream*

00:06:01.249 --> 00:06:07.649
OK, that one’s not actually a ghost, it’s
a spell set by Mad Eye Moody in order to scare

00:06:07.649 --> 00:06:11.919
off Death Eaters from raiding the House of
Black while the order is away.

00:06:11.919 --> 00:06:16.830
But there are some creepy ghosts at Hogwarts,
such as Helena Ravenclaw.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:23.340
In life, Helena was the daughter of Rowena
Ravenclaw, the founder of the Ravenclaw house.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:28.020
After running away from Hogwarts, Helena’s
mother became extremely ill and sent the Bloody

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.089
Baron, who was in love with Helena, to retrieve
her.

00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:36.319
Not wanting to go with the Baron, Helena refused,
and in a rage, the Baron killed her, leaving

00:06:36.319 --> 00:06:40.990
her bitter and angry at everyone outside of
her own house and earning her the nickname,

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:42.520
The Grey Lady.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:47.050
In fact, the rest of Hogwarts doesn’t even
believe that Helena’s ghost can speak, because

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:51.090
she’s only been known to talk to Ravenclaws
from time to time.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:56.110
Her quiet, shy and serene nature makes it
all the more terrifying when you try to confront

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.979
her, and witness one of her outbursts.

00:06:57.979 --> 00:07:00.659
"I know what he's done.

00:07:00.659 --> 00:07:03.349
I know who he is!

00:07:03.349 --> 00:07:04.960
He defiled it!

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.569
With dark magic!"

00:07:06.569 --> 00:07:10.819
The last ghost that I’m going to talk about
is not creepy in a horror sense, but I do

00:07:10.819 --> 00:07:13.050
feel that she deserves a mention.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:17.020
Moaning Myrtle is the ghost of a student who
haunts the second-floor girl’s lavatory

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:18.020
at Hogwarts.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:23.110
She was the lone student killed in during
the occurences of the 1943 school year in

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:27.849
which the Chamber of Secrets was open the
monster was set free by Tom Riddle.

00:07:27.849 --> 00:07:32.569
Myrtle isn’t really a scary ghost per say,
but she is creepy in her own way.

00:07:32.569 --> 00:07:37.399
Her reckless emotions and are enough that
nobody ever goes into the bathroom she inhabits,

00:07:37.399 --> 00:07:41.170
and she has a strange fascination with death
for someone stuck in the mental state of a

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.170
14 year old.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:46.159
“I was just sitting in the U-Bend thinking
about death.”

00:07:46.159 --> 00:07:50.619
Myrtle is more seen as creepy because she
doesn’t really know boundaries, and from

00:07:50.619 --> 00:07:55.050
what we can gather, she’s kind of a weird
kid even before death and tends to make the

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.500
students uncomfortable.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:08:01.749
But Moaning Myrtle is really just trivial
compared to our next moment of horror.

00:08:01.749 --> 00:08:02.749
“Tonight.

00:08:02.749 --> 00:08:11.039
He who betrayed his friends whose heart rots
with murder shall break free.

00:08:11.039 --> 00:08:20.330
Innocent blood shall be spilt, and servant
and master shall be reunited once more.”

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:25.080
Yep, just another day in divinations class
with Professor Trelawney.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:29.539
But the creepy thing here is not Professor
Trelawney, but rather the array of visions

00:08:29.539 --> 00:08:32.680
that happen throughout Voldemort’s rise
to power.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:37.720
Most of them are visions that appear to Harry
because of his connection with Lord Voldemort.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:42.300
Imagine how horrifying it must be to know
that at any time you might be yanked out of

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:47.340
the here and now and sucked into a nightmarish
image of the world’s most powerful dark

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:50.760
force, who by the way, wants to kill you.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:55.890
The visions get more and more creepy as Lord
Voldemort starts to realize that he and Harry

00:08:55.890 --> 00:09:00.840
are connected and starts to show him things
on purpose, in order to get into his head.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:05.440
There is also a pretty scary scene at the
end of Order of the Phoenix, in which Voldemort

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:10.620
takes over Harry’s body entirely in order
to deliver a message to Dumbledore.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:15.820
“You’ve lost old man.”

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.130
"AH!"

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:20.370
One of the things that makes this universe
scary is the fact that powerful creatures

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.870
can be found roaming about freely with no
real safe havens.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:28.510
The muggles have no idea that dangerous magical
creatures could be among them at any time.

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:33.090
There are two example of such creatures made
most prominent in Harry Potter and the Prisoner

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:37.710
of Azkaban, animagus and werewolves.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.910
"Werewolves?"

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.910
Both are creatures with human forms and the
ability to transform into beasts.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:47.720
The main difference, as taught by Professor
Snape when he substitutes teaching Defense

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:52.430
Against the Dark Arts, is that Animagus have
control over their transformations and have

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:56.990
the ability to turn into a wider variety of
animals; whereas werewolves will transform

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:01.570
against their will and will always transform
into a beast similar to a wolf.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:04.770
Both can be quite creepy in their own ways.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:09.100
Animagus have control over their actions,
so clever planning can be used to trick an

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.570
unsuspecting victim who thinks they are just
dealing with an animal.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:17.630
It should be mentioned many Animagus are not
evil, but it is also common for criminals

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:21.490
to take advantage of the ability to escape
the law.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:23.830
Werewolves can be scary for the opposite reason.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:28.010
Though they may be perfectly good people in
their human forms, when full moon hits, they

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:32.580
lose control and attempt to bite or kill anyone
they can get their paws on.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:35.180
Werewolves also have one of the scariest forms.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:39.710
While they do resemble regular wolves, their
long gangly limbs are a transformation from

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:43.710
what we would naturally expect, causing the
werewolves to look like a terrifying cross

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.740
between man and wolf.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:50.320
Combine that with their sharp carnivorous
teeth, empty glowing eyes, and the fact that

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:54.640
they appear at night and you have some of
the most dangerous creatures the world has

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.050
to offer.

00:10:56.050 --> 00:11:00.250
We do have more creatures to discuss, but
it’s not just creepy monsters that Harry

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:02.320
and his friends have to deal with.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:06.230
One of the first creepy places that Harry
visits is Knockturn Alley.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:10.690
Harry accidentally travels there before his
second year when he mispronounces Diagon Alley

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.820
and is taken there instead.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:17.950
Like Diagon Alley, Knockturn Alley is a shopping
center, but the shops are dedicated to the

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.010
dark arts.

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:25.230
As you can imagine, this draws in an interesting
crowd of characters -- not the crowd you want

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:28.300
to fall in with before you start your second
year of school.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:29.370
“Come with us.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:33.440
We’ll help you find your way back.”

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.170
But Knockturn Alley isn’t just a mall for
misfit wizards.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:42.000
When Harry, Ron and Hermione return to Knockturn
Alley before their 6th year, they eavesdrop

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:46.560
on some kind of ritual going on at a store
called Borgin and Burke’s which appears

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.630
to be Draco Malfoy’s initiation as a Death
Eater.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:54.570
Borgin and Burke’s is also the store where
Tom Riddle got his first job after leaving

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:55.860
Hogwarts.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.790
Other notable locations in Knockturn Alley
include a shop that sells materials related

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:04.840
to raising the dead, a shop that sells bones
and a shop that sells shrunken heads.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:09.200
The Alley is creepy not only because of it’s
morbid nature, but mostly because of the horrible

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.880
people it can attract.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:15.830
The next item is actually a cursed object
that Harry encounters almost immediately upon

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.590
arriving at Knockturn Alley.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:23.110
I’m referring to the Hand of Glory, a severed
human hand skeleton with the power to immobilise

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:26.450
those who catch it’s gaze and unlock doors.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:30.950
This is because the hand is said to have belong
to an executed master criminal.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:35.040
It only makes a small cameo appearance in
the film adaptation of Harry Potter and the

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:40.030
Chamber of Secrets, but with that in mind,
Harry is lucky to have ever escaped it’s

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.030
grasp.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:45.040
The chilling thing about these objects are
the rumors of how they are created, with many

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:50.090
myths claiming that an executed criminals
blood is used to animate the hand.

00:12:50.090 --> 00:12:54.200
Stick around, because after the break, I’ll
be discussing an even more shocking object

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.690
that Harry encounters during his time at Hogwarts.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:06.850
In order to gain more information about Nicolas
Flamel, the creator of the Philosopher's Stone,

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:13.130
Harry sneaks into the restricted section of
the library, where this happens.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:20.550
*screams of agony*

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:24.380
The impact of the jump scare is multiplied
by the fact that Harry is sneaking around

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:28.520
and we’re thinking more about not getting
caught than something scaring us.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:33.240
The agonized face to go along with it in the
film adaptation also adds to the effect.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:38.560
Later on, towards the end of that first year,
Harry and the gang go to retrieve the stone,

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:43.440
and after getting past the aforementioned
Fluffy, find themselves in another trap.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.060
Devil’s Snare.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.970
This is a plant with magical properties.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:51.490
It wraps around it’s victim and the level
of it’s constriction is determined by panic

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:53.100
level of the victim.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:56.300
If the victim relaxes, the snare will relax
it’s grip.

00:13:56.300 --> 00:14:01.460
They thrive in dark damp environments, making
it the perfect trap for a dungeon.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:06.160
Devil’s snare prays on the fear of claustrophobia,
with a critical twist.

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:11.330
As fear intensifies, so does the threat, creating
an endless cycle of increasing danger if one

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.430
cannot compose themselves while caught in
the snare.

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:19.810
This is easier said than done, since those
who suffer from the anxiety disorder of claustrophobia

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:27.580
often have symptoms including panic attacks
or fear of suffocation.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:32.700
Hogwarts is a 10th century gothic-style castle
which in many cases can be creepy in its own

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:33.700
right.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.220
But I’d also like to explore some of the
other creepy locations in the series.

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:39.160
The triwizard maze.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:42.910
During Harry’s fourth year at Hogwarts,
a interscholastic competition known as the

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:47.800
Tri-Wizard tournament is held, and the final
task is to navigate the triwizard maze, an

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:50.600
enormous hedge maze with 20 foot hedges.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.720
Prior to the contestants entering the maze,
Dumbledore offers them a word of caution.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.990
“You see, people change in the maze.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:15:04.500
Oh, find the cup if you can, but be very wary:
you could just lose yourselves along the way.”

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:09.070
This fits in with the themes of maturation
that arise after the triwizard tournament.

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:12.980
The students are growing up into adults and
changing to face the harsh realities of the

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:14.290
real world.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:19.180
However, as in life, the contestants are not
only finding themselves changing, for better

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:22.350
or for worse, but the world around them is
changing as well.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:27.790
The maze has the ability to reconfigure itself,
and those who are not able to adapt are sucked

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.029
into its grasp and defeated.

00:15:30.029 --> 00:15:34.980
In this way, the maze combines the fear of
growing up, gerascophobia, with the fear of

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:39.740
getting lost to create a terrifying trial
for the young wizards.

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:42.660
I think we’ve all been creeped out by the
idea something living with within our walls

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:47.570
at one point or another -- and if not -- I’m
sure everyone’s gotten a chill from an abandoned

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:49.530
location at some point.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.620
These are two reasons why I find The Chamber
of Secrets to be the creepiest location in

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:54.870
Hogwarts.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:58.970
The Chamber of Secrets is an ancient system
of pipes under the school that house the monster

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:03.779
of slytherin, which of course, I’ll touch
back on and analyse later in this video.

00:16:03.779 --> 00:16:08.300
The chamber is so well hidden that even the
teachers and staff cannot find it and do not

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.360
believe with full certainty that it exists.

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:15.720
The chamber can be accessed by activating
the correct sink tap while speaking the phrase

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.780
“open up” in parseltongue.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:21.550
After navigating a series of caves filled
with skeletons and sewage pipes, they comes

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:24.030
across the door to the inner chamber.

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:28.180
Another line of snake-speak grants access
to an enormous pathway lined with vicious

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:33.281
looking snake head statues and a statue at
the end of an old man’s face, whom I can

00:16:33.281 --> 00:16:38.580
only assume is Salazar Slytherin, the founder
of the house and designer of the chamber.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:43.710
Salazar was prejudiced against mud-bloods,
or wizards with muggle parents, so knowing

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:48.580
the chamber was some kind of lair for… those
kind of people… adds an additional factor

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:50.720
of unsettling atmosphere.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:54.980
There are so many reasons the chamber of secrets
is scary.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.650
Primarily, snakes.

00:16:56.650 --> 00:17:00.290
If you find snakes creepy, this is not the
place for you.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.400
Isolation is another reason.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:06.709
When Harry and Ron are down there, nobody
knows where they are, so unlike their previous

00:17:06.709 --> 00:17:09.730
adventures, no teacher would be able to bail
them out.

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.929
The third reason, is anticipation.

00:17:11.929 --> 00:17:15.909
The horror of the contents of the chamber
is built up over the course of their second

00:17:15.909 --> 00:17:20.220
year, with creepy messages being left and
scary stories circulating.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:24.110
Finally, the true contents of the chamber
are unknown.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:28.929
All Harry knows is that it’s rumored, and
probably does contain a monster, so he’s

00:17:28.929 --> 00:17:31.100
always on edge during his visit.

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:35.090
If you think The Chamber of Secrets seems
like an unsafe place for school-children,

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:39.369
you won’t even want to begin to explore
The Forbidden Forest.

00:17:39.369 --> 00:17:43.960
Also known as the dark forest, this dangerous
sprawling woodland could be the subject of

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:47.669
it’s very own video -- but in order to keep
things brief, let’s just touch on a few

00:17:47.669 --> 00:17:49.200
of the things that can be found here.

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.679
Keep in mind, this is directly adjacent to
the school.

00:17:52.679 --> 00:17:58.749
There’s no fence, there’s no spell keeping
anything in or out, it’s just considered

00:17:58.749 --> 00:17:59.990
off-limits.

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:06.399
The forest is home to acromantulas, thestrals,
unicorns, centaurs, werewolves, hippogriffs

00:18:06.399 --> 00:18:12.570
and… after the events of year one -- Fluffy,
but during the events of year one, Lord Voldemort.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:16.450
Did I mention this is right next to the school?

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:22.570
I would never be able to sleep at night knowing
I was this close to such a dangerous location.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:26.369
But The Forbidden Forest isn’t the only
dangerous location that’s right next to

00:18:26.369 --> 00:18:32.881
the school -- stay tuned to hear about the
other one.

00:18:32.881 --> 00:18:37.169
The Great Lake is a relatively small freshwater
lake that houses a couple of the creepiest

00:18:37.169 --> 00:18:39.529
creatures in Harry Potter lore.

00:18:39.529 --> 00:18:44.059
As if if the close proximity to Hogwarts wasn’t
enough, it’s also linked to the school’s

00:18:44.059 --> 00:18:45.179
drain system.

00:18:45.179 --> 00:18:48.039
The lake contains a couple species of creepy
sea-creatures.

00:18:48.039 --> 00:18:49.039
Merpeople.

00:18:49.039 --> 00:18:55.019
I know mermaids and horror are not often associated
with each other, but these mermaids are not

00:18:55.019 --> 00:19:00.220
your typical hot girl attached to a fishtail,
they are more like extremely scary fish with

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.340
a somewhat humanoid form.

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:06.950
Oh, and did I mention they have sharp teeth
and sharper pitchforks?

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.070
And they sound like this.

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.070
“Wha!

00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:11.820
Only one.”

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:16.720
But the merpeople are really the least of
Harry’s concerns during his underwater trial

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.269
in the Tri-Wizard tournament.

00:19:18.269 --> 00:19:23.320
At the bottom of the lake, lies a great evil
known as Grindylow.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:29.389
If merpeople are half man, half fish, then
grindylow more like half demon, half octopus,

00:19:29.389 --> 00:19:31.549
and the result is terrifying.

00:19:31.549 --> 00:19:36.840
They are typically just under 5 feet tall,
making an encounter with one pretty scary

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:42.179
on it’s own, but these creatures dwell at
the bottom of the lake and attack in swarms.

00:19:42.179 --> 00:19:47.059
They are described as sickly green creatures
with horns, and yes, they are actually considered

00:19:47.059 --> 00:19:48.059
demons.

00:19:48.059 --> 00:19:52.860
They mostly survive on eating fish or algae,
but they are known to eat humans from time

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:53.860
to time.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:58.230
They supposedly have very strong fingers,
with which they strangle their prey.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:03.080
But perhaps even more haunting, the grindylow
are depicted in folk tales to grab little

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:08.989
children standing near the edge of the lake
and pull them down to drown them before feasting

00:20:08.989 --> 00:20:12.129
on their insides.

00:20:12.129 --> 00:20:13.610
Horcruxes.

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:17.149
Like the dark forest -- the horcruxes are
a huge topic to cover.

00:20:17.149 --> 00:20:20.799
These objects are cursed with a spell that
puts part of the caster inside of the object,

00:20:20.799 --> 00:20:24.129
so that he may not be killed unless the object
is destroyed.

00:20:24.129 --> 00:20:28.239
Lord Voldemort has seven of them, which is
a lot considering this process can only be

00:20:28.239 --> 00:20:30.649
initiated by killing another wizard.

00:20:30.649 --> 00:20:34.929
The objects themselves are not what I consider
creepy (besides the snake, that one’s a

00:20:34.929 --> 00:20:38.720
straight nope) but the essences of Voldemort
that are released with the destruction of

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:40.519
each one can be pretty off-putting.

00:20:40.519 --> 00:20:58.070
"I've seen your heart and it is mine."

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:02.250
Perhaps the most creepy instance of this,
and one of the creepiest images in the series

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:06.769
overall, is the second to last horcrux, Harry
Potter himself.

00:21:06.769 --> 00:21:11.490
Harry must allow Voldemort to kill him in
order to kill the bit of Voldemort that resides

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:12.870
inside of him.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:16.990
Harry is taken to the afterlife, where we
see this fragment of the dark lord that binds

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:22.830
he and Harry together, finally die off.

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:26.519
*breathing*

00:21:26.519 --> 00:21:27.520
Professor Snape.

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:28.870
Well, OK.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:31.650
Professor Snape isn’t actually that creepy
in the end.

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:36.240
But his mannerisms have been known to intimidate
students, earning him a reputation.

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:39.200
“Neville, what frightens you most of all?”

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:40.200
“Pr..fe...ss…

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:41.200
Sn..”

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.200
“Sorry?”

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.200
“Professor Snape.”

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.240
“Professor Snape, yes.”

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:49.799
As time goes on, however, this fear does become
less laughable due to the ever-decreasing

00:21:49.799 --> 00:21:54.950
faith the heroes have in Snape’s loyalty
to Dumbledore, the frightening power he displays

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:58.660
and his duty as a triple agent keeping tabs
on the Death Eaters.

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:03.470
Snape’s harsh nature and particular disdain
for Harry Potter may have stemmed from his

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:07.919
past, being bullied by Harry’s father, and
his unrequited love for Harry’s mother.

00:22:07.919 --> 00:22:14.309
Lily’s death could help explain his dislike
for light and hopeless demeanor.

00:22:14.309 --> 00:22:24.710
“Turn to page 394.”

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:28.379
Did you know?

00:22:28.379 --> 00:22:34.220
The Mirror of Erised is named as such because
Erised is the mirror image of the word desire.

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:37.940
Dumbledore tells Harry that the happiest person
would look in the mirror and see nothing but

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:39.080
their own reflection.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:42.980
The mirror shows the deepest desire of whoever
gazes into it.

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:47.429
Harry spends many nights revisiting the mirror
to see the image of himself with his parents.

00:22:47.429 --> 00:22:51.970
Although this sounds like a happy time of
reflection, the mirror may actually be a great

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:54.450
danger to its user.

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:01.610
“This mirror gives us neither knowledge
or truth.

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:07.200
Men have wasted away in front of it.

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:09.490
Even gone mad.”

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:14.980
To me, this is one of the creepiest objects
in the Wizarding World because of these implications.

00:23:14.980 --> 00:23:16.730
Monsters are scary, sure.

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:20.110
But the Mirror of Erised reflects more of
a psychological horror.

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:25.090
The mirror presents the user’s greatest
desire regardless of if the desire is an attainable

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:26.860
goal or a fantasy.

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:31.529
The euphoria produced by looking into the
mirror is so strong that it starts to become

00:23:31.529 --> 00:23:32.809
addictive.

00:23:32.809 --> 00:23:38.289
It dangles an often unattainable goal before
those who look into, and may cause them to

00:23:38.289 --> 00:23:40.740
lose track of what’s real, and what’s
fantasy.

00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:45.239
Once this happens, the person is as good as
trapped -- trapped in their own mind without

00:23:45.239 --> 00:23:47.990
knowledge or desire to get out.

00:23:47.990 --> 00:23:52.200
Perhaps the scariest part though, is that
those with the greatest ambition, are most

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:54.419
vulnerable to it.

00:23:54.419 --> 00:23:59.119
The next topic is something unlikely to ever
appear to anyone in the mirror.

00:23:59.119 --> 00:24:00.340
Acromantula.

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:06.700
These giant spiders grow over 15 feet long,
possess giant pincers, contain extremely toxic

00:24:06.700 --> 00:24:12.360
venom, and like all too many of the species
I’ve discussed, love the taste of human

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:13.559
flesh.

00:24:13.559 --> 00:24:17.730
As if that wasn’t already enough, these
creatures are intelligent, and we know at

00:24:17.730 --> 00:24:21.429
the very least, that colony leaders are capable
of speech.

00:24:21.429 --> 00:24:24.919
Their ability to communicate, however, does
not make them any less savage.

00:24:24.919 --> 00:24:30.990
“My sons and daughters do not harm Hagrid
on my command.

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:39.280
But I cannot deny them fresh meat when it
wanders so willingly into our midst.

00:24:39.280 --> 00:24:41.480
Goodbye, friend of Hagrid.”

00:24:41.480 --> 00:24:43.690
“Can we panic now?”

00:24:43.690 --> 00:24:47.350
Yes, that would be an appropriate time to
panic.

00:24:47.350 --> 00:24:51.169
Even given their former leader’s alliance
with Hagrid, the Acromantula attempt to eat

00:24:51.169 --> 00:24:56.220
Hagrid right after Aragog’s death and still
take the more powerful side of Voldemort during

00:24:56.220 --> 00:24:58.369
the final battle for Hogwarts.

00:24:58.369 --> 00:25:01.399
They don’t even make an exception for their
own kind.

00:25:01.399 --> 00:25:05.309
When one dies, the colony eats the corpse
until nothing remains.

00:25:05.309 --> 00:25:10.749
I can appreciate resourcefulness, but the
very idea of an acromantula funeral sends

00:25:10.749 --> 00:25:11.749
shivers.

00:25:11.749 --> 00:25:16.220
I can only imagine how Ron Weasley feels about
all of this.

00:25:16.220 --> 00:25:19.600
One year after his first encounter with the
colony in the dark forest, his greatest fear

00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:28.809
is revealed during Professor Lupin’s defense
against the dark arts class.

00:25:28.809 --> 00:25:33.580
*music*

00:25:33.580 --> 00:25:43.240
So the Acromantula encounter is sure to be
one of the scariest moments for Ron, but make

00:25:43.240 --> 00:25:50.440
sure to keep watching, because up next is
a creature that even they are terrified of.

00:25:50.440 --> 00:25:58.200
Earlier on in this video, I mentioned that
the Chamber of Secrets is home to the monster

00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:01.600
of Slytherin -- which Harry assumed was Aragog.

00:26:01.600 --> 00:26:06.320
What he eventually found upon entering the
chamber was that something even more nightmarish

00:26:06.320 --> 00:26:09.529
was within the walls of the castle all along.

00:26:09.529 --> 00:26:15.639
The monster is the Basilisk, a massive 50
foot serpent monster with the power to kill

00:26:15.639 --> 00:26:20.149
anyone who it makes direct eye contact with
it, or petrify those who make indirect eye

00:26:20.149 --> 00:26:21.149
contact.

00:26:21.149 --> 00:26:26.320
It’s fangs are so venomous, that they are
one of the only known materials powerful enough

00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:28.470
to destroy a horcrux.

00:26:28.470 --> 00:26:33.470
The basilisk is intelligent, cunning and like
other serpents, has the ability to speak to

00:26:33.470 --> 00:26:35.570
those wizards who understand Parseltongue.

00:26:35.570 --> 00:26:39.549
It’s voice, makes your skin crawl.

00:26:39.549 --> 00:26:40.860
“Blood.

00:26:40.860 --> 00:26:44.770
I smell blood.

00:26:44.770 --> 00:26:50.000
Let me rip you.

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:55.220
Let me kill you.

00:26:55.220 --> 00:26:56.520
Kill…

00:26:56.520 --> 00:26:57.830
Kill.

00:26:57.830 --> 00:26:59.140
KILL!”

00:26:59.140 --> 00:27:03.279
Salazar Slytherin, who left Hogwarts shortly
after co-founding it due to a disagreement

00:27:03.279 --> 00:27:09.080
over the acceptance of mudbloods, created
the chamber deep under the school before departing.

00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:14.330
It was so well hidden that teachers began
to accept the idea that it was just a myth.

00:27:14.330 --> 00:27:19.330
“Well naturally the school has been searched
many times.

00:27:19.330 --> 00:27:22.200
No such chamber has been found.”

00:27:22.200 --> 00:27:26.029
When Tom Riddle discovered the chamber as
a Hogwarts student, he was able to the control

00:27:26.029 --> 00:27:29.919
the Basilisk, because he was the last remaining
heir of Slytherin.

00:27:29.919 --> 00:27:34.919
He turned it against the school, hurting many,
and killing one student, Myrtle Warren, who

00:27:34.919 --> 00:27:37.429
would later be known as Moaning Myrtle.

00:27:37.429 --> 00:27:41.970
Since it was Riddle who committed this crime,
he was able to create the first horcrux, using

00:27:41.970 --> 00:27:46.989
his dairy, which preserved his state at the
time until the next time the Chamber was opened:

00:27:46.989 --> 00:27:51.799
Harry Potter’s second year, when Harry Ron
and Hermione decide to investigate.

00:27:51.799 --> 00:27:54.999
“And it will be dangerous.

00:27:54.999 --> 00:27:56.279
Very dangerous.”

00:27:56.279 --> 00:28:00.700
The Basilisk is one of the scariest monsters
in the Wizarding World even without the influence

00:28:00.700 --> 00:28:02.960
of a dark lord controlling it.

00:28:02.960 --> 00:28:07.390
Snakes are already creepy creatures to begin
with, turning it into a giant 50 foot monster

00:28:07.390 --> 00:28:09.159
is no exception.

00:28:09.159 --> 00:28:13.240
Tom Riddle’s diary takes control of Ginny
Weasley to write foreboding warning on the

00:28:13.240 --> 00:28:18.580
walls across Hogwarts and eventually taking
her prisoner to feed off her life force.

00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:23.159
Feeding off an eleven year old’s life force
will always be creepy in my mind.

00:28:23.159 --> 00:28:27.809
When Harry and Ron get closer to rescuing
her, the discover the giant molted snake skin.

00:28:27.809 --> 00:28:30.049
That’s not a pleasant thought either.

00:28:30.049 --> 00:28:35.009
Harry manages to blind the beast, but that
just makes it even more terrifying somehow,

00:28:35.009 --> 00:28:38.179
because it uses sound to continue to track
Harry.

00:28:38.179 --> 00:28:42.659
But the scariest part in my opinion, is when
Hermione discovers the method by the which

00:28:42.659 --> 00:28:45.379
the Basilisk gets around the school.

00:28:45.379 --> 00:28:46.379
“Pipes?

00:28:46.379 --> 00:28:49.389
It’s using the plumbing?”

00:28:49.389 --> 00:28:54.149
What makes this so very unsettling is that
his actually happens in real life.

00:28:54.149 --> 00:28:58.700
If you have plumbing in your home, you are
at risk of snakes using that to get into your

00:28:58.700 --> 00:29:01.529
house and attack you while you’re using
the bathroom.

00:29:01.529 --> 00:29:04.759
This could happen at any time.

00:29:04.759 --> 00:29:09.159
When the snake has a deadly magical stare,
that fear is doubled or tripled, which is

00:29:09.159 --> 00:29:12.879
why I believe that Harry’s second year had
to be one of the scariest throughout his time

00:29:12.879 --> 00:29:15.119
at Hogwarts.

00:29:15.119 --> 00:29:20.580
I’ve already made several references to
Voldemort’s followers, the Death Eaters,

00:29:20.580 --> 00:29:25.250
a group pure-blood supremacists who have sworn
their allegiance to the dark lord.

00:29:25.250 --> 00:29:29.929
Like the Basilisk, it is their similarities
to real world prejudice groups that make them

00:29:29.929 --> 00:29:33.340
creepy, along with their familiarity with
the dark arts.

00:29:33.340 --> 00:29:37.799
Despite everything that happens in the first
three years of Harry’s time at Hogwarts,

00:29:37.799 --> 00:29:41.769
things are relatively under control compared
to the chaos that would later be set at the

00:29:41.769 --> 00:29:46.749
Quidditch World Cup in 1994 and everything
that took place after.

00:29:46.749 --> 00:29:51.659
The dark pointed robes and torches send a
clear message that this group is back, and

00:29:51.659 --> 00:29:56.899
the fact that an entire fanbase of wizards
are scared off or killed by the Death Eaters

00:29:56.899 --> 00:30:00.690
is a testament to how feared they actually
are.

00:30:00.690 --> 00:30:05.220
In the Voldemort revival ritual, the Death
Eaters take on a cult like form and use dark

00:30:05.220 --> 00:30:08.389
magic of which Harry has never seen the likes.

00:30:08.389 --> 00:30:13.090
Like many of the real world groups they are
based on, they use fear as a tactic to claim

00:30:13.090 --> 00:30:15.110
and retain their power.

00:30:15.110 --> 00:30:19.410
One of the most frightening scenes in the
entire series takes place during year 5 at

00:30:19.410 --> 00:30:21.190
the Department of Mysteries.

00:30:21.190 --> 00:30:25.690
The Death Eaters use their attire, in addition
to a voice modulation spell, to ramp up the

00:30:25.690 --> 00:30:28.720
fear of the unknown that exist within all
of us.

00:30:28.720 --> 00:30:30.200
“Where’s Sirius?”

00:30:30.200 --> 00:30:37.909
“You know you really should learn to tell
the difference.

00:30:37.909 --> 00:30:41.309
Between dreams.

00:30:41.309 --> 00:30:44.700
And reality.”

00:30:44.700 --> 00:30:49.669
We another fear tactic they use is the disruption
of order.

00:30:49.669 --> 00:30:54.309
Order gives us comfort and security, so by
creating chaos, the Death Eaters instill fear

00:30:54.309 --> 00:30:56.730
in massive amounts of people at one time.

00:30:56.730 --> 00:31:01.380
Here’s one moment I found particularly disturbing,
where the Death Eaters create chaos at Bill

00:31:01.380 --> 00:31:02.720
Weasley's wedding.

00:31:02.720 --> 00:31:05.009
“The ministry has fallen.

00:31:05.009 --> 00:31:07.679
The Minister of Magic is dead.

00:31:07.679 --> 00:31:13.499
They are coming.

00:31:13.499 --> 00:31:19.309
They are coming.”

00:31:19.309 --> 00:31:25.950
Of course, it would be impossible to open
a discussion about the Death Eaters without

00:31:25.950 --> 00:31:28.710
also mentioning the Dark Lord himself.

00:31:28.710 --> 00:31:35.630
Lord Voldemort.

00:31:35.630 --> 00:31:39.419
Tom Riddle is a true psychopath even from
an early age.

00:31:39.419 --> 00:31:44.359
Flashback scenes to his childhood reveal his
cold, evil persona and his ruthless thirst

00:31:44.359 --> 00:31:45.840
for power.

00:31:45.840 --> 00:31:50.570
Like his forefather Salazar Slytherin before,
he sets out to purge those who he does not

00:31:50.570 --> 00:31:52.259
consider pure-bloods.

00:31:52.259 --> 00:31:57.540
His lack of empathy is truly chilling, and
his rise to power is so forceful that most

00:31:57.540 --> 00:32:01.619
wizards are too afraid to even mutter his
true name.

00:32:01.619 --> 00:32:06.730
If not for his encounter with Lily Potter,
it is possible he may have never been stopped.

00:32:06.730 --> 00:32:11.399
But this important night drastically weakened
Voldemort, forcing him to take on a new persona,

00:32:11.399 --> 00:32:15.600
hiding the in the shadows, and committing
vile acts to stay alive, like slurping the

00:32:15.600 --> 00:32:20.429
cursed blood of the unicorn just for pure
life energy.

00:32:20.429 --> 00:32:22.529
*growl*

00:32:22.529 --> 00:32:24.619
"AHH!"

00:32:24.619 --> 00:32:29.940
The transformation and revival had adverse
effects on Voldemort.

00:32:29.940 --> 00:32:34.619
With each atrocity he committed using the
dark arts, he became more serpent-like, losing

00:32:34.619 --> 00:32:40.850
his hair, flattening his nose, transforming
his voice and making him somewhat of a human

00:32:40.850 --> 00:32:41.850
monster.

00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:46.960
With each passing year after his revival,
he becomes more and more powerful, and more

00:32:46.960 --> 00:32:48.899
and more disturbing.

00:32:48.899 --> 00:32:52.340
It does seem like a lot of his power comes
from fear though.

00:32:52.340 --> 00:32:57.279
His reputation becomes so great that many
of his opponents have psychologically already

00:32:57.279 --> 00:32:58.279
lost.

00:32:58.279 --> 00:33:02.820
The Minister of Magic himself, refuses to
admit that Voldemort is back even when all

00:33:02.820 --> 00:33:06.630
the evidence is there because he is in such
great denial.

00:33:06.630 --> 00:33:11.010
One of the only factors that eventually lead
to his defeat is the fact Harry starts a movement

00:33:11.010 --> 00:33:14.669
to get Hogwarts students to call Voldemort
by his real name.

00:33:14.669 --> 00:33:18.820
Without this tide being turned over the course
of Harry’s education, it’s hard to imagine

00:33:18.820 --> 00:33:22.539
the Hogwarts students standing any chance
during the final battle.

00:33:22.539 --> 00:33:26.019
Voldemort's greatest asset is really fear
itself.

00:33:26.019 --> 00:33:31.190
However, there are three more creatures that
I’ve determined to be even more terrifying

00:33:31.190 --> 00:33:38.889
than Lord Voldemort, so be sure to keep watching
to find out what makes them so scary.

00:33:38.889 --> 00:33:47.849
Before getting the final three, let’s go
over a couple of honorable mentions.

00:33:47.849 --> 00:33:49.509
Tom Riddle’s graveyard.

00:33:49.509 --> 00:33:50.590
Classic spooky graveyard.

00:33:50.590 --> 00:33:51.659
Gotta love it.

00:33:51.659 --> 00:33:54.929
The animatronics in the Weasley twins’ shop.

00:33:54.929 --> 00:33:57.049
Absolutely nightmare fuel.

00:33:57.049 --> 00:34:04.230
Getting possessed by a cursed necklace.

00:34:04.230 --> 00:34:10.400
*screaming*

00:34:10.400 --> 00:34:14.500
And also this one painting in Prisoner of
Azkaban and then just the fact that Luna Lovegood

00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:17.370
keeps raw meat in her purse...?

00:34:17.370 --> 00:34:18.840
OK.

00:34:18.840 --> 00:34:19.840
Final three.

00:34:19.840 --> 00:34:23.270
The creepiest things I’ve found in the Harry
Potter Franchise.

00:34:23.270 --> 00:34:24.580
Boggarts.

00:34:24.580 --> 00:34:28.590
This shape-shifting species takes the form
of of its opponent’s greatest fear.

00:34:28.590 --> 00:34:32.520
That means Boggarts can take the shape of
everything I just mentioned so far in this

00:34:32.520 --> 00:34:34.210
video and everything I will mention.

00:34:34.210 --> 00:34:38.770
In this regard, they are even scarier than
Lord Voldemort, because if someone has something

00:34:38.770 --> 00:34:42.980
they fear more than the Dark Lord, Boggarts
can take that shape as well.

00:34:42.980 --> 00:34:45.620
There is really no need to analyse this one.

00:34:45.620 --> 00:34:49.179
Whatever your fear is, they will find, and
they will become it.

00:34:49.179 --> 00:34:53.710
I also find it kind of eerie that nobody has
actually seen the true form of a Boggart,

00:34:53.710 --> 00:34:57.170
because once you’ve seen one, it’s shape
has already been shifted.

00:34:57.170 --> 00:35:01.790
Even a Boggart looking in a mirror would theoretically
become its own worst fear.

00:35:01.790 --> 00:35:06.230
I suppose someone could plant a camera, but
as far as I know, nobody has.

00:35:06.230 --> 00:35:10.300
But I can only imagine that default form is
extremely disturbing.

00:35:10.300 --> 00:35:15.080
There are only a couple reasons why boggarts
aren’t the number one scariest thing.

00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:19.400
First, you can outnumber them, assuming your
partner doesn’t have the same fear that

00:35:19.400 --> 00:35:21.950
you have, only one would be affected.

00:35:21.950 --> 00:35:25.870
Second, the size of the boggart is limited
to the size of the room they are in.

00:35:25.870 --> 00:35:29.660
And third, assuming that you know that you
are up against the boggart and not the real

00:35:29.660 --> 00:35:33.190
thing, you can use a Riddikulus charm to vastly
weaken it.

00:35:33.190 --> 00:35:34.190
“Riddikulus!”

00:35:34.190 --> 00:35:38.960
We’ve already talked about dark wizards
like the Death Eaters and Lord Voldemort and

00:35:38.960 --> 00:35:42.630
there’s only one type of wizard that is
more horrifying than a dark wizard.

00:35:42.630 --> 00:35:50.690
A dark wizard that has risen from the dead.

00:35:50.690 --> 00:35:53.910
Dark wizards have a spell used to reanimate
the corpses of the dead.

00:35:53.910 --> 00:35:58.140
You may recall that there was a shop dedicated
to necromancy in Knockturn Alley.

00:35:58.140 --> 00:36:02.970
However, the appearances of the Inferi are
much more alarming than what comes to mind

00:36:02.970 --> 00:36:04.760
when I think of a zombie.

00:36:04.760 --> 00:36:09.280
Many of them are in a deep state of decay,
revealing bone structures, but also containing

00:36:09.280 --> 00:36:12.510
some old traces of skin, hair and flesh.

00:36:12.510 --> 00:36:17.270
To explain why we find these and similar morbid
creatures scary, I’ll refer to something

00:36:17.270 --> 00:36:22.310
known as the Uncanny Valley theory, an idea
that the human brain is trained to recognize

00:36:22.310 --> 00:36:27.450
and process other human faces, but when there
are alterations, we find them disturbing,

00:36:27.450 --> 00:36:29.280
because we know that it’s wrong.

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:33.550
The cloudy white eyes also suggest that the
corpse is not cognisant.

00:36:33.550 --> 00:36:37.190
Remember when trolls were the scariest thing
Harry had to worry about?

00:36:37.190 --> 00:36:40.570
Oh what can change in 6 short years.

00:36:40.570 --> 00:36:46.520
I was also going to include Harry’s encounter
the year after with Bathilda Bagshot at Godric’s

00:36:46.520 --> 00:36:51.100
Hollow, but upon further investigation, that
doesn’t count, because the corpse wasn’t

00:36:51.100 --> 00:36:53.950
animated using a spell, but it’s the same
idea.

00:36:53.950 --> 00:36:54.950
[Clip]

00:36:54.950 --> 00:36:58.530
At this point, you probably already know the
scariest creature in all of the Wizarding

00:36:58.530 --> 00:36:59.530
World.

00:36:59.530 --> 00:37:01.390
Let’s give this some context.

00:37:01.390 --> 00:37:04.750
When Harry encounters the boggart in Professor
Lupin’s defense against against the dark

00:37:04.750 --> 00:37:09.503
art class, his biggest fear isn’t Voldemort,
the man who killed his parents who he’s

00:37:09.503 --> 00:37:12.800
been hearing about for the better part of
the last three years now.

00:37:12.800 --> 00:37:19.750
No, Harry’s biggest fear is a Dementor,
a creature he only once encountered very recently

00:37:19.750 --> 00:37:25.630
and briefly on the train, but had such a terrifying
experience with -- it surpassed even his battle

00:37:25.630 --> 00:37:30.410
with the Voldemort controlled Professor Quirrell
and his life-threatening experiences with

00:37:30.410 --> 00:37:33.270
the Basilisk or Acromantula.

00:37:33.270 --> 00:37:37.970
Unlike every other student in the class, Harry
is not even given the opportunity to face

00:37:37.970 --> 00:37:42.040
his fear before Professor Lupin steps in to
save him.

00:37:42.040 --> 00:37:46.000
The Dementors are floating black-cloaked wraith-like
creatures.

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:51.400
Their almost featureless faces are not often
seen, and contain only large hole with which

00:37:51.400 --> 00:37:57.860
the suck the soul out their victim, an experience
said be worse than death.

00:37:57.860 --> 00:38:02.590
The Dementors are first dispatched from their
post guarding Azkaban in order to find and

00:38:02.590 --> 00:38:05.630
capture the escapee, Sirius Black.

00:38:05.630 --> 00:38:09.990
They surround Hogwarts during Harry, Ron and
Hermione’s third year.

00:38:09.990 --> 00:38:14.470
Harry first encounters one on the train, where
for some unknown reason, it attempts to suck

00:38:14.470 --> 00:38:15.910
out his soul.

00:38:15.910 --> 00:38:20.160
Upon arriving at Hogwarts, Professor Dumbledore
offers this warning.

00:38:20.160 --> 00:38:23.080
“A word of caution.

00:38:23.080 --> 00:38:24.830
Dementors are vicious creatures.

00:38:24.830 --> 00:38:29.700
They will not distinguish between the one
they hunt and the one who gets in their way…

00:38:29.700 --> 00:38:36.640
Therefore I must warn each and every one of
you to give them no reason to harm you.”

00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:41.490
But the Dementor appearances become more frequent
throughout the school year.

00:38:41.490 --> 00:38:46.910
Their very presence causes the plant life
around them to immediately shrivel and die.

00:38:46.910 --> 00:38:53.110
They exude a radius of cold lifelessness,
enough to freeze nearby water that they pass

00:38:53.110 --> 00:38:54.110
by.

00:38:54.110 --> 00:38:58.890
A Quidditch match nearly ends in disaster
when Harry is once again targeted by several

00:38:58.890 --> 00:39:02.750
Dementors while chasing the snitch up in the
clouds during a storm.

00:39:02.750 --> 00:39:07.800
There is only one known spell that can repel
them, and it’s very difficult to pull off,

00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:12.700
but Harry is able to perform a Patronus charm
to ward off a spiraling swarm of them and

00:39:12.700 --> 00:39:15.440
save Sirus at the end of the year.

00:39:15.440 --> 00:39:20.870
Harry claims that the Dementors force you
to relive your worst nightmares, in his case,

00:39:20.870 --> 00:39:24.190
the final cries of his parents being murdered
by Voldemort.

00:39:24.190 --> 00:39:28.830
Up to that point, Harry already considers
the Dementors to be the scariest encounter

00:39:28.830 --> 00:39:33.120
of his life -- and that’s while they’re
technically still on his side trying to find

00:39:33.120 --> 00:39:35.040
Sirius Black.

00:39:35.040 --> 00:39:40.190
But things get even scarier for Harry when
he is ambushed by two Dementors in the muggle

00:39:40.190 --> 00:39:44.780
world before his fifth year -- a place where
he is supposed to be relatively safe from

00:39:44.780 --> 00:39:46.400
magical beings.

00:39:46.400 --> 00:39:51.410
Not long after, the allegiance of the Dementors
was thrown even more into question after a

00:39:51.410 --> 00:39:53.280
mass breakout from Azkaban.

00:39:53.280 --> 00:39:58.610
It would not be long before Harry’s worst
enemy joined Voldemort and the Death Eaters

00:39:58.610 --> 00:40:00.050
in the battle.

00:40:00.050 --> 00:40:04.210
I think another reason the Dementors are as
unsettling as they are, besides having the

00:40:04.210 --> 00:40:09.460
most sinister appearance of any other species,
is the fact that they serve as guards.

00:40:09.460 --> 00:40:13.520
Everyone has broken the rules at some point
as a kid and been punished for it, so everyone

00:40:13.520 --> 00:40:17.560
can relate to this fear of getting caught
by these dark authority figures, even if they

00:40:17.560 --> 00:40:20.310
know that they haven’t done anything wrong.

00:40:20.310 --> 00:40:25.200
When the punisher is 10 foot reaper like creature
who suck the light and happiness out of the

00:40:25.200 --> 00:40:31.130
air, sense your fear and feast on your soul…
well there isn’t anything that could conceivably

00:40:31.130 --> 00:40:32.790
be worse than that.

00:40:32.790 --> 00:40:37.880
It’s scary to think that many believe the
Dementors are too severe a punishment for

00:40:37.880 --> 00:40:40.910
prisoners in Azkaban, some of the worst criminals
in the world.

00:40:40.910 --> 00:40:47.010
If they can’t handle the torture of a dementor,
it’s hard to believe that anyone could.

00:40:47.010 --> 00:40:52.010
One of the most chilling aspects, that once
a Dementor has sucked your soul, you may go

00:40:52.010 --> 00:40:57.540
on living as an empty shell… never experiencing
happiness again…

00:40:57.540 --> 00:41:02.300
Dementors are Rowling’s manifestation of
a deep, unrecoverable depression....

00:41:02.300 --> 00:41:08.200
Unlike Voldemort… they will never go away.

00:41:08.200 --> 00:41:13.590
Thank you for sticking to the end of this
video.

00:41:13.590 --> 00:41:16.900
Let me know in the comments if there are any
creepy things in the Wizarding World that

00:41:16.900 --> 00:41:21.000
I failed to mention, and be sure to give me
your ideas on what non-horror franchise I

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:24.130
could cover in the next episode of creepy
things.

00:41:24.130 --> 00:41:27.510
My name is CZ and if you love horror you’re
in the right place.

00:41:27.510 --> 00:41:32.280
On this channel I videos on a variety of horror
topics like Things You Missed in horror movies

00:41:32.280 --> 00:41:36.840
and Al Dente Creepypasta, where I write and
narrate my own scary stories.

00:41:36.840 --> 00:41:42.500
Dumbledore would like to remind you to subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:41:42.500 --> 00:41:48.360
that deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:41:48.360 --> 00:41:50.320
Assuming we both survive.

